  {t="T", seg=5, q={65}, names={"The Defias Brotherhood"}, text="Wiley the Black, upstairs in the inn. Do not take his follow-up (The Defias Brotherhood, back to Westfall).", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=21.4, y=45.4},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={92}, names={"Redridge Goulash"}, text="Chef Breanna, in the house west of the inn", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=17.6, y=43.8},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={3741}, names={"Hilary's Necklace"}, text="Glinting Mud lies under water along the lake shore on both sides of the bridge (spots between 14 and 33, 51-56). Open the piles until one holds Hilary's Necklace.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=25.2, y=54.2, path={{20.5,54.0}}},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={125}, names={"The Lost Tools"}, text="Swim east from the bridge. The Sunken Chest with Oslow's Toolbox lies on the lake bottom. Murlocs (17-20) swim around it: kill what comes at you before you dive, and keep the fish they drop (Spotted Sunfish for Selling Fish).", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=36.4, y=54.7},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={3741}, names={"Hilary's Necklace"}, text="Hilary, the girl next to Shawn", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=24.2, y=53.6},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={125}, names={"The Lost Tools"}, text="Foreman Oslow", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=27.1, y=48.6},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={89}, names={"The Everstill Bridge"}, text="Foreman Oslow", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=27.1, y=48.6},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={89}, names={"The Everstill Bridge"}, text="The data lists the gnolls north of Lakeshire as the source of Iron Pikes and Iron Rivets: Redridge Brutes (17-18) in the camps around 24, 35 and Redridge Mystics (18-19) a little further north. Take the path north out of town. Earth Shock the Mystics when they cast, pull one camp member at a time, Stoneclaw Totem if two come. Do not go deeper than you need: Bashers (19-20) are behind them. Great Goretusks on the way drop snouts for the goulash.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=24.0, y=34.8},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={246,98407}, names={"Assessing the Threat","Show of Force"}, text="Cross the bridge again and work the gnoll camps south and south-west of Lakeshire, toward Three Corners. Kill 10 Redridge Mongrels (15-16) and 6 Redridge Poachers (16-17, mostly in the southern camps around 29, 80), and every Redridge Thrasher (14-15) you see until you have 5 Spiked Collars. Poachers shoot: run up to them. Drop Earthbind Totem when a gnoll runs at low health. Tarantulas (15-16) and Great Goretusks (16-17) live between the camps: kill them as you go for 5 Crisp Spider Meat and 5 Great Goretusk Snouts (Redridge Goulash).", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=20.0, y=70.0},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={129}, names={"A Free Lunch"}, text="Guard Parker at Three Corners", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=10.2, y=71.5},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={130}, names={"Visit the Herbalist"}, text="Guard Parker", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=10.2, y=71.5},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={127}, names={"Selling Fish"}, text="10 Spotted Sunfish from murlocs. Murloc Shorestrikers (16-17) on the south shore of the lake around 44, 69 are the easiest; Minor Tidecallers and Flesheaters (17-19) live further along the shore and in the water. This is a level 21 quest: pull single murlocs from the edge of a camp, Earth Shock the Tidecallers' heals and drop Earthbind Totem, because they run and bring friends. Keep every Murloc Fin you loot: Dockmaster Baren asks for 8 of them in the next segment. The condors for the goulash are next.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=43.7, y=69.2},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={92}, names={"Redridge Goulash"}, text="Redridge Goulash: the 5 Tough Condor Meat come from Dire Condors (18-19), which fly over the hills south and east of the lake, close to the murloc shore. Fight them one at a time with full health. If you still miss Crisp Spider Meat or Goretusk Snouts, Tarantulas and Great Goretusks are around Three Corners and all along the road back to Lakeshire.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=47.7, y=56.9},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={246}, names={"Assessing the Threat"}, text="Deputy Feldon", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=25.6, y=60.0},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={98407}, names={"Show of Force"}, text="Deputy Feldon", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=25.6, y=59.9},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={89}, names={"The Everstill Bridge"}, text="Foreman Oslow, north end of the bridge", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=27.1, y=48.6},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={127}, names={"Selling Fish"}, text="Dockmaster Baren", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=22.6, y=47.4},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={130}, names={"Visit the Herbalist"}, text="Martie Jainrose, the herbalist on the west side of town", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=16.8, y=46.3},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={131}, names={"Delivering Daffodils"}, text="Martie Jainrose", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=16.8, y=46.3},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={92}, names={"Redridge Goulash"}, text="Chef Breanna", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=17.6, y=43.8},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={131}, names={"Delivering Daffodils"}, text="Darcy in the inn", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=21.5, y=44.3},
  {t="FLY", seg=5, arg="Stormwind", text="Ariena Stormfeather, south of the bridge"},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={120}, names={"Messenger to Stormwind"}, text="From the gryphon master walk through the Trade District to the Valley of Heroes, the bridge inside the main gate. General Marcus Jonathan sits on his horse there.", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=69.2, y=82.7},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={121}, names={"Messenger to Stormwind"}, text="General Marcus Jonathan. Keep it: you are back in Lakeshire in the next segment.", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=69.2, y=82.7},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={118}, names={"The Price of Shoes"}, text="Walk out of the gate and down the road to Goldshire (two minutes). Smith Argus works in the smithy.", zone="Elwynn Forest", map=1429, x=41.7, y=65.5},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={119}, names={"Return to Verner"}, text="Smith Argus. Keep the Crate of Horseshoes for the next segment.", zone="Elwynn Forest", map=1429, x=41.7, y=65.5},
  {t="N", seg=5, arg="Walk back into Stormwind and take the Deeprun Tram to Ironforge", text="The tram station is in the Dwarven District."},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=5, text="Ironforge: Eldrun Stormbreaker (47.6, 13.5). Learn your level 18 spells. Call of Water needs level 20: you come back for it."},
  {t="FLY", seg=5, arg="Thelsamar", text="Gryth Thurden, the gryphon master in the middle of Ironforge"},
  {t="S", seg=5, arg="Thelsamar", text="Innkeeper Hearthstove in the Stoutlager Inn. Buy food and water here."},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={436}, names={"Ironband's Excavation"}, text="Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar (37.2, 47.4)", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=37.2, y=47.4},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={263}, names={"In Defense of the King's Lands"}, text="Follow the road south past the Valley of Kings tower and turn east into the Stonesplinter Valley. Kill what is still missing of 10 Stonesplinter Shamans and 10 Bonesnappers (15-16). Earth Shock the Shamans' casts.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=33.0, y=80.0, path={{39.8,50.4},{39.8,53.4},{43.2,60.0},{43.2,63.6},{41.0,66.9},{41.0,70.2},{38.0,74.4},{34.8,74.4},{33.0,75.9}}},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={263}, names={"In Defense of the King's Lands"}, text="Mountaineer Wallbang in the southern guard tower", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=23.5, y=74.5},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={217}, names={"In Defense of the King's Lands"}, text="Captain Rugelfuss, in the same tower", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=23.2, y=73.7},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={86585}, names={"Banner of the Fallen"}, text="Back in the Stonesplinter Valley: the body of Mountaineer Ylva lies at 31.7, 86.4 (new in Forever)", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=31.7, y=86.4},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={86585}, names={"Banner of the Fallen"}, text="Use the Banner of Ironforge next to the body. The trogg Headsplitter comes for it: kill him. Clear the troggs around the spot first so nothing joins the fight.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=32.2, y=86.4},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={217}, names={"In Defense of the King's Lands"}, text="Grawmug (17) and his guards Gnasher and Brawler (16) stand together in the cave at the very back of the valley (34.8, 90.5). Clear the cave on the way in. Then drop Stoneclaw Totem, kill the two guards first and Grawmug last, with Healing Wave when you drop below half.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=34.7, y=90.6, path={{34.4,84.1}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={217}, names={"In Defense of the King's Lands"}, text="Captain Rugelfuss", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=23.2, y=73.7},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={86585}, names={"Banner of the Fallen"}, text="Captain Rugelfuss", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=23.1, y=73.8},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={353}, names={"Stormpike's Delivery"}, text="Run the road north through Thelsamar to the northern guard tower. Mountaineer Stormpike is in the tower (24.8, 18.4).", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=24.8, y=18.4, path={{24.9,70.5},{24.9,66.3},{27.6,61.8},{27.6,57.6},{30.4,53.4},{30.0,43.3},{32.2,38.5},{29.8,22.6},{27.2,18.4}}},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={250}, names={"A Dark Threat Looms"}, text="Chief Engineer Hinderweir VII, in the middle of the Stonewrought Dam at the north end of the loch", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=46.0, y=13.6},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={250}, names={"A Dark Threat Looms"}, text="Walk east along the dam and down the eastern ramp. The Suspicious Barrel stands at 56.1, 13.2 with two Dark Iron Sappers (17) next to it: kill them one after the other.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=56.1, y=13.2},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={199}, names={"A Dark Threat Looms"}, text="From the Suspicious Barrel", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=56.1, y=13.2},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={199}, names={"A Dark Threat Looms"}, text="Back to Chief Engineer Hinderweir.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=46.0, y=13.6},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={161}, names={"A Dark Threat Looms"}, text="Chief Engineer Hinderweir: A Dark Threat Looms. The powder goes to Dun Modr in the north of the Wetlands. Do not go now: the route is there at level 30, keep it in your log until then", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=46.0, y=13.6},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={2039}, names={"Find Bingles"}, text="Go back down the eastern ramp and follow the east shore of the loch south. Bingles Blastenheimer stands by his broken flying machine. Stay on the shore: the Mo'grosh ogres in the hills north-east of the loch are elite.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=63.6, y=47.9, path={{43.2,14.5},{43.0,17.8},{47.4,20.8},{52.8,30.4},{59.2,31.3},{60.4,33.1},{65.2,33.1},{66.2,34.6},{66.2,41.5}}},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={2038}, names={"Bingles' Missing Supplies"}, text="Bingles Blastenheimer. You collect his tools after the lodge.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=63.6, y=47.9},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={385}, names={"Crocolisk Hunting"}, text="Keep south-east to the Farstrider Lodge. Marek Ironheart is inside.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=81.8, y=61.7},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={86758}, names={"Twisting the Knife"}, text="Marek Ironheart: Twisting the Knife (new in Forever)", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=81.8, y=61.6},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={257}, names={"A Hunter's Boast"}, text="Daryl the Youngling, in the lodge. This starts a 15 minute timer.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=83.5, y=65.5},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={257}, names={"A Hunter's Boast"}, text="Kill 6 Mountain Buzzards (15-16). They fly over the hills right outside the lodge, south and west of it.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=75.3, y=73.4, path={{79.3,66.0},{77.9,67.8},{77.9,71.1}}},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={257}, names={"A Hunter's Boast"}, text="Daryl the Youngling", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=83.5, y=65.5, path={{77.9,71.1},{77.9,67.8},{79.3,66.0}}},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={258}, names={"A Hunter's Challenge"}, text="Daryl the Youngling. A 12 minute timer: no detours.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=83.5, y=65.5},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={258}, names={"A Hunter's Challenge"}, text="Kill 5 Elder Mountain Boars (16-17). They roam north-west of the lodge, on the slopes toward Bingles (around 66, 40). Run straight there, kill five and run straight back.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=63.5, y=38.7},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={258}, names={"A Hunter's Challenge"}, text="Daryl the Youngling", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=83.5, y=65.5},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={385,86758}, names={"Crocolisk Hunting","Twisting the Knife"}, text="Go back to the east shore. Loch Crocolisks (14-15) lie along the shore and in the shallows from Bingles north: kill them for 5 Crocolisk Meat and 6 Crocolisk Skins. Daggerfang, the crocolisk for Marek's knife, hunts along the same shore (seen between 59 and 66, 34-55). Do not touch the Large Loch Crocolisk (22 elite).", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=61.9, y=44.7},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={2038}, names={"Bingles' Missing Supplies"}, text="Swim out to the islands in the north of the loch. Three toolbuckets hold the Wrench (48.7, 30.1), the Screwdriver (48.4, 20.5) and the Hammer (51.8, 24.1); the Blastencapper lies at 54.2, 26.6. Crocolisks swim between the islands.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=51.0, y=25.0, path={{62.8,43.6},{62.8,39.1},{60.4,33.4},{59.0,31.3},{52.8,30.4}}},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={2038}, names={"Bingles' Missing Supplies"}, text="Back to Bingles Blastenheimer on the east shore", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=63.6, y=47.9, path={{53.2,30.7},{59.2,31.3},{60.4,33.1},{65.2,33.1},{66.2,34.6},{66.2,41.5}}},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={385}, names={"Crocolisk Hunting"}, text="Marek Ironheart at the Farstrider Lodge", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=81.8, y=61.7},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={86758}, names={"Twisting the Knife"}, text="Marek Ironheart", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=81.8, y=61.6},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={436}, names={"Ironband's Excavation"}, text="The dig is south-west of the lodge. Magmar Fellhew stands in the camp above it.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=64.9, y=66.7},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={297}, names={"Gathering Idols"}, text="Magmar Fellhew", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=64.9, y=66.7},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={298}, names={"Excavation Progress Report"}, text="Prospector Ironband, next to him. Just a letter for Thelsamar.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=65.9, y=65.6},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={86613}, names={"Excavation Tools"}, text="Excavation Tools (new in Forever). The quest starts from the Excavation Tools you pick up inside the dig; the data has no exact spots. Look for tool sets on the ground while you kill troggs, and pick up six. If you find none, press Skip here and on its hand-in.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=70.2, y=64.5},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={297,86613}, names={"Gathering Idols","Excavation Tools"}, text="Go down into the dig. Stonesplinter Geomancers (17-18), Diggers (18-19) and Berserk Troggs (19-20) drop the 8 Carved Stone Idols. Earth Shock the Geomancers' fire spells, pull from the edge and keep Stoneclaw Totem for a second trogg. Collect the six tool sets while you are down there.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=70.2, y=64.5},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={297}, names={"Gathering Idols"}, text="Magmar Fellhew", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=64.9, y=66.7},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={86613}, names={"Excavation Tools"}, text="Prospector Ironband", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=65.9, y=65.6},
  {t="L", seg=5, lvl=20, text="Only if you are not close to 20 yet (the step ticks by itself at 20). Call of Water needs level 20 and you want it on the Ironforge trip that comes next. The two hand-ins on the way back to Thelsamar give about 3,000 XP with the kills on the way: if your level 19 bar reads less than about 18,200 / 21,300, kill troggs in the dig (17-20) until it does, then press Skip. Expect to need 25 to 30 kills.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=70.2, y=64.5},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={86614}, names={"Silver of the Waves"}, text="Walk west along the south end of the loch and up its west shore. The Discarded Fishing Toolbox lies on the shore at 48.8, 54.0 (new in Forever).", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=48.8, y=54.0},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={86614}, names={"Silver of the Waves"}, text="Khara Deepwater, the fishing trainer on the shore north-east of Thelsamar (40.4, 39.4)", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=40.4, y=39.4},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={298}, names={"Excavation Progress Report"}, text="Jern Hornhelm in Thelsamar", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=37.2, y=47.4},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={301}, names={"Report to Ironforge"}, text="Jern Hornhelm", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=37.2, y=47.4},
  {t="FLY", seg=5, arg="Ironforge", text="Thorgrum Borrelson in Thelsamar. You must be level 20 now."},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={301}, names={"Report to Ironforge"}, text="Prospector Stormpike in the Hall of Explorers", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=74.6, y=11.7},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={302}, names={"Powder to Ironband"}, text="Prospector Stormpike", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=74.6, y=11.7},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={94494}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Eldrun Stormbreaker, your shaman trainer: Call of Water (needs level 20)", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=47.6, y=13.5},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={971}, names={"Knowledge in the Deeps"}, text="Gerrig Bonegrip in the Forlorn Cavern. The Lorgalis Manuscript is under water in the first big pool inside.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=50.8, y=5.6, dg=4},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=5, text="Ironforge: Eldrun Stormbreaker (47.6, 13.5). Learn your level 20 spells. Ghost Wolf is the important one: use it for every long run outdoors from now on."},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={2041}, names={"Speak with Shoni"}, text="Gnoarn the gnome (ForeverChanges shows him at 62.2, 29.2; Questie has him in Tinker Town at 69.2, 50.6). A letter for Stormwind, handed in in the next segment.", zone="Ironforge", map=1455, x=62.2, y=29.2},
  {t="FLY", seg=5, arg="Thelsamar", text="Gryth Thurden"},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={302}, names={"Powder to Ironband"}, text="Jern Hornhelm", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=37.2, y=47.4},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={273}, names={"Resupplying the Excavation"}, text="Jern Hornhelm", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=37.2, y=47.4},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={468}, names={"Report to Mountaineer Rockgar"}, text="Mountaineer Kadrell walks the road through Thelsamar (needs level 19)", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=34.2, y=47.8},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={273}, names={"Resupplying the Excavation"}, text="Huldar waits on the road south of the loch (52.2, 69.3), on the way to the dig", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=52.2, y=69.3},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={454}, names={"After the Ambush"}, text="Huldar", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=52.2, y=69.3},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={454}, names={"After the Ambush"}, text="Miran, next to him", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=52.2, y=69.4},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={309}, names={"Protecting the Shipment"}, text="Miran. This starts an escort to the excavation site.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=52.2, y=69.4},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={309}, names={"Protecting the Shipment"}, text="Walk with Miran. Dark Iron dwarves ambush the cart on the way: let them come to you, drop Stoneclaw Totem and kill them one at a time. Miran must survive.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=52.2, y=69.4},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={309}, names={"Protecting the Shipment"}, text="Prospector Ironband at the excavation camp", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=65.9, y=65.6, path={{52.2,66.0},{55.0,62.1},{56.6,62.1},{58.4,64.2}}},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={94494}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Ghost Wolf back around the south end of the loch, through Thelsamar and north. Norric Lochthane lives in the house on the north-west shore, just before the dam.", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=41.9, y=19.0},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={94495}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Norric Lochthane", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=41.9, y=19.0},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={468}, names={"Report to Mountaineer Rockgar"}, text="Mountaineer Rockgar guards the Dun Algaz tunnel in the north-west corner of Loch Modan (25.4, 10.4)", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=25.4, y=10.4, path={{36.0,11.8},{26.0,11.5}}},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={455}, names={"The Algaz Gauntlet"}, text="Mountaineer Rockgar", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=25.4, y=10.4},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={455}, names={"The Algaz Gauntlet"}, text="Follow the road through the Dun Algaz tunnels into the Wetlands. Dragonmaw Scouts (19-20) and Grunts (20-21) stand along the road and in the side camps: kill 8 Scouts and 6 Grunts on the way through. They hit hard for your level: one at a time, Earthbind Totem for runners, Healing Wave between pulls. Whatever is missing you can finish in segment 7.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=48.6, y=77.0},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={94495}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Where the road leaves the hills, turn east and follow the foot of the southern cliffs to the waterfalls that drop from the Stonewrought Dam. Hervdana Saegrund lives in a cave beneath the falls (65.7, 76.4). Mosshide Gnolls and Mongrels (20-22) roam the marsh on the way and Dark Iron Insurgents (18-19) stand near the cave: go around what you can in Ghost Wolf.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=65.7, y=76.4},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={94497}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Hervdana Saegrund", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=65.7, y=76.4},
  {t="C", seg=5, q={94497}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Go down to the pool at the bottom of the waterfalls, right below her cave, and use the Empty Brown Waterskin at the water.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=65.7, y=76.4},
  {t="T", seg=5, q={94497}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Hervdana Saegrund", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=65.7, y=76.4},
  {t="A", seg=5, q={94499}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Hervdana Saegrund. The Empty Red Waterskin is filled at Stonewatch Falls in Redridge in the next segment: keep it in your bags.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=65.7, y=76.4},
  {t="H", seg=5, arg="Thelsamar", text="Hearthstone back to the inn"},
  {t="FLY", seg=6, arg="Ironforge", text="Thorgrum Borrelson in Thelsamar"},
  {t="N", seg=6, arg="Look for a Bronze Tube in Ironforge", text="Viktori in Darkshire needs one Bronze Tube for Look to the Stars. Engineers make it: check the auction house, and ask Gearcutter Cogspinner, the engineering supplier in Tinker Town (67.8, 42.5), on your way to the tram. Not verified: the quest data only lists drops from machines and a vendor in Thousand Needles, so a city supplier stocking one is Classic knowledge. Without a tube you skip the Look to the Stars steps later."},
  {t="N", seg=6, arg="Take the Deeprun Tram to Stormwind", text="The tram station is in Tinker Town."},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={2041}, names={"Speak with Shoni"}, text="Shoni the Shilent, in the Dwarven District a few steps from the tram exit. Do not take her follow-up (Deadmines). Billibub Cogspinner, the engineering supplier, stands close by (62.4, 29.9): ask him for a Bronze Tube too, and try the Stormwind auction house.", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=62.6, y=34.1},
  {t="FLY", seg=6, arg="Lakeshire", text="Dungar Longdrink, the gryphon master in the Trade District"},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={119}, names={"Return to Verner"}, text="Cross the bridge. Verner Osgood, on the town side.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=25.9, y=47.3},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={122,124}, names={"Underbelly Scales","A Baying of Gnolls"}, text="Verner Osgood", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=25.9, y=47.3},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={98386}, names={"Alther's Mill"}, text="Foreman Oslow at the north end of the bridge: Alther's Mill (new in Forever)", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=27.1, y=48.5},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={20}, names={"Blackrock Menace"}, text="Marshal Marris, a few steps east of the bridge", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=28.4, y=49.0},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={98387}, names={"Blackrock Blockade"}, text="Marshal Marris: Blackrock Blockade (new in Forever)", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=28.3, y=48.8},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={121}, names={"Messenger to Stormwind"}, text="Magistrate Solomon in the town hall", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=24.9, y=44.5, path={{28.2,46.9},{26.4,44.2}}},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={91}, names={"Solomon's Law"}, text="Bailiff Conacher, in the town hall too", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=24.6, y=44.3},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={150}, names={"Murloc Poachers"}, text="Dockmaster Baren on the dock (needs level 20)", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=22.6, y=47.4},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={34}, names={"An Unwelcome Guest"}, text="Martie Jainrose, the herbalist on the west side of town. Bellygrub is level 24: you kill him last, after the big loop.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=16.8, y=46.3},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={124}, names={"A Baying of Gnolls"}, text="Take the path north out of Lakeshire. Kill 10 Redridge Brutes (17-18, the first camps around 24, 35) and 8 Redridge Mystics (18-19, further up around 24, 29). Earth Shock the Mystics' casts. Do not chase Yowler deeper in the hills: that quest is for a later segment.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=24.1, y=32.0, path={{15.7,46.3},{14.1,42.1},{19.1,35.5},{23.3,35.2}}},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={98386}, names={"Alther's Mill"}, text="Go back down and follow the north shore of the lake east to Alther's Mill. Kill 12 Greater Tarantulas (19-20) and destroy 6 Tarantula Eggs around the mill. Stoneform removes their poison. Leave Chatter, the rare elite spider that walks here, alone.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=50.4, y=41.1, path={{24.3,37.9},{30.0,44.8},{39.6,39.4},{40.6,36.1},{42.2,36.1},{44.2,39.1}}},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={91}, names={"Solomon's Law"}, text="Keep east into Galardell Valley. Shadowhide gnolls drop the 10 Shadowhide Pendants. Stay at the mouth of the valley, where Rabid Shadowhide Gnolls (21-22) and Shadowhide Gnolls (22-23) stand around 69, 50; the Brutes, Warriors, Slayers and Darkweavers deeper in are 23-26. They are above your level: pull one at a time from far away, Earth Shock every fight, Stoneclaw Totem as soon as a second gnoll comes, and drink to full before each pull.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=69.0, y=50.2},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={94499}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Call of Water. Stonewatch Falls drops into the pool at the south-east end of the valley. The Murloc Nightcrawlers (21-22) live at its foot, around 76, 59. Kill the ones near the water (they drop Murloc Fins too), stand at the foot of the falls and use the Empty Red Waterskin. The quest names the spot only as \"Stonewatch Falls near the Nightcrawler Murlocs\": the coordinates are where the data puts those murlocs.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=76.1, y=59.5, path={{71.6,55.2},{77.1,55.8},{77.9,58.8}}},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={20,98387}, names={"Blackrock Menace","Blackrock Blockade"}, text="Leave the valley the way you came and go south. Blackrock Grunts (19-20) and Outrunners (20-21) camp on the slopes south-east of the lake, below Stonewatch Keep; Renegades (21-22) are mixed in. They drop the 10 Battleworn Axes. The 8 Stolen Weapons and 10 Blackrock Supplies are in the same camps (new quest: the giver says \"south-east below Stonewatch Keep\" and the data has no exact spots, so look for things to click in the camps and loot every orc). Stay out of Stonewatch Keep itself: the Scouts, Sentries and Shadowcasters there are elite. Earthbind Totem stops orcs from running for help.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=58.0, y=62.0, path={{77.9,58.8},{77.1,55.8},{68.8,55.2},{66.8,59.4},{64.8,59.4},{62.0,62.4},{59.0,60.0}}},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={150}, names={"Murloc Poachers"}, text="Follow the lake shore back west. Murlocs along the south-east shore (Flesheaters, Tidecallers, Scouts, 18-20) drop the Murloc Fins: you need 8, counting the ones you already carry.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=47.3, y=60.9},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={122}, names={"Underbelly Scales"}, text="Black Dragon Whelps (17-18) fly over the hills south of the lake, between the murloc shore and Lakeshire. Kill them until you have 6 Underbelly Whelp Scales. Earth Shock their fireballs.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=38.6, y=67.4},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={20}, names={"Blackrock Menace"}, text="Back in Lakeshire: Marshal Marris. Do not take the follow-up, Tharil'zun (elite).", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=28.4, y=49.0},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={98387}, names={"Blackrock Blockade"}, text="Marshal Marris", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=28.3, y=48.8},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={98386}, names={"Alther's Mill"}, text="Foreman Oslow", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=27.1, y=48.6},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={122,124}, names={"Underbelly Scales","A Baying of Gnolls"}, text="Verner Osgood. Do not take Howling in the Hills yet.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=25.9, y=47.3},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={150}, names={"Murloc Poachers"}, text="Dockmaster Baren", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=22.6, y=47.4},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={91}, names={"Solomon's Law"}, text="Bailiff Conacher in the town hall", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=24.6, y=44.3},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={34}, names={"An Unwelcome Guest"}, text="Bellygrub (24), a big boar, roots around in the fields west of Lakeshire, past Martie's garden (10.6, 49.3). Fight him with full health and mana: Stoneclaw Totem down first, Earth Shock on cooldown, Healing Wave at half health. If he gets you low, run back toward the town guards.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=10.6, y=49.3},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={34}, names={"An Unwelcome Guest"}, text="Martie Jainrose", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=16.8, y=46.3},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={386}, names={"What Comes Around..."}, text="Guard Berton in Lakeshire. The head of Targorr the Dread.", zone="Redridge Mountains", map=1433, x=26.3, y=46.6, dg=3},
  {t="F", seg=6, arg="Darkshire", text="Take the road south-west to Three Corners and from there the road south into Duskwood. It leads straight to Darkshire. Stay on the road in Ghost Wolf. Felicia Maline, the gryphon master, stands on the east side of town.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=77.5, y=44.3},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={163,164,165}, names={"Raven Hill","Deliveries to Sven","The Hermit"}, text="Elaine Carevin, at the south end of town", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.3, y=48.7},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={56}, names={"The Night Watch"}, text="Commander Althea Ebonlocke, in front of the town hall", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.5, y=46.8},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={96139}, names={"The Valor Family"}, text="Sirra Von'Indi in the town hall: The Valor Family (new in Forever)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.6, y=47.5},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={101}, names={"The Totem of Infliction"}, text="Madame Eva, in the house on the north side of the square. You collect her parts over the whole Duskwood trip.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=45.3},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={174}, names={"Look To The Stars"}, text="Viktori Prism'Antras, in the house at the east end of town. Only with a Bronze Tube in your bags. Without one press Skip here and on every Look to the Stars step that follows in this segment.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=79.8, y=48.0},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={174}, names={"Look To The Stars"}, text="Viktori Prism'Antras: hand over the Bronze Tube", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=79.8, y=48.0},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={175}, names={"Look To The Stars"}, text="Viktori Prism'Antras", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=79.8, y=48.0},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={175}, names={"Look To The Stars"}, text="Blind Mary lives in the lone house south of Darkshire (82.0, 59.1)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=82.0, y=59.1},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={177}, names={"Look To The Stars"}, text="Blind Mary. The Insane Ghoul is level 26: you fight him at the end of the segment, when you are back at her house.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=82.0, y=59.1},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={56}, names={"The Night Watch"}, text="Tranquil Gardens Cemetery is just south of Mary's house. Kill 8 Skeletal Warriors (21-22) and 6 Skeletal Mages (22-23). Earth Shock the Mages' casts. Loot everything: they drop Skeleton Fingers for Madame Eva (you need 10). Keep away from the chapel for now, the Insane Ghoul is inside.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=79.4, y=70.8},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={245}, names={"Eight-Legged Menaces"}, text="Take the road west along the south side of Duskwood. Watcher Dodds stands on it, about halfway (45.1, 67.0). From here on kill the spiders you pass: Pygmy Venom Web Spiders (18-19) count for him, and every spider can drop Vials of Spider Venom for Madame Eva (5) and Gooey Spider Legs. Keep 6 Gooey Spider Legs for a later quest. Stoneform cures their poison. You hand this in when you pass Dodds again.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=45.1, y=67.0, path={{69.8,70.2},{67.0,64.8},{65.2,63.6},{64.4,58.2},{50.6,60.0},{49.2,61.8},{45.6,62.7}}},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={163}, names={"Raven Hill"}, text="Jitters hides in Raven Hill, the dead village in the west (18.4, 56.4)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=18.4, y=56.4, path={{45.0,63.3},{43.6,61.2},{36.8,59.4},{32.4,53.4},{25.0,52.8},{22.7,56.4}}},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={5}, names={"Jitters' Growling Gut"}, text="Jitters", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=18.4, y=56.4},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={96139}, names={"The Valor Family"}, text="Search Raven Hill for the Raven Hill Tome. New quest: the data has no exact spot, only \"search Raven Hill\". Look inside the ruined houses and around the village for a book you can click.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=18.4, y=56.4},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={164}, names={"Deliveries to Sven"}, text="Sven Yorgen camps on the western edge of Duskwood, north-west of Raven Hill (7.8, 34.1)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=7.8, y=34.1, path={{15.7,55.2},{10.5,48.7},{9.3,40.9},{7.3,37.6}}},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={95}, names={"Sven's Revenge"}, text="Sven Yorgen", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=7.8, y=34.1},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={226}, names={"Wolves at Our Heels"}, text="Lars, at the same camp", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=7.7, y=33.2},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={95}, names={"Sven's Revenge"}, text="Sven's farm is in the south of the zone, south of Watcher Dodds. Go back along the south road (Ghost Wolf) and click the Mound of loose dirt behind the tree stump at the farm (49.9, 77.7). Zzarc'Vul's ogres (around 37, 81, west of the farm) are far above your level: keep away from their mound.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=49.9, y=77.7, path={{8.3,31.3},{13.1,29.8},{16.3,26.8},{28.4,30.1},{32.2,35.8},{32.2,50.4},{32.6,53.4},{34.8,57.0},{36.8,59.4},{40.0,60.6},{46.8,61.8},{52.8,60.9},{53.6,62.1},{53.6,66.0},{51.4,69.3},{52.4,74.4}}},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={230}, names={"Sven's Camp"}, text="From the mound", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=49.9, y=77.7},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={245}, names={"Eight-Legged Menaces"}, text="Finish the 15 Pygmy Venom Web Spiders (18-19) in the woods around the farm and along the south road.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=10.4, y=55.5, path={{52.4,74.4},{51.4,69.3},{53.6,66.0},{52.8,60.9},{46.8,61.8},{37.4,59.7},{32.4,53.4},{25.8,52.8},{24.3,50.4},{11.5,50.7},{10.5,52.2}}},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={245}, names={"Eight-Legged Menaces"}, text="Watcher Dodds, back on the road north-west of the farm", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=45.1, y=67.0, path={{10.5,52.2},{11.5,50.7},{24.3,50.4},{25.8,52.8},{32.4,53.4},{36.8,59.4},{43.6,61.2},{45.0,63.3}}},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={226}, names={"Wolves at Our Heels"}, text="Cut north-west through the woods toward the north side of Raven Hill Cemetery. Kill 12 Starving Dire Wolves (19-20) and 8 Rabid Dire Wolves (20-21): both roam the northern half of western Duskwood.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=30.0, y=28.0, path={{45.0,63.3},{43.6,61.2},{36.8,59.4},{32.6,53.4},{32.4,31.6}}},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={165}, names={"The Hermit"}, text="Abercrombie the hermit lives in the shack north of Raven Hill Cemetery (28.1, 31.5)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=28.1, y=31.5},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={148}, names={"Supplies from Darkshire"}, text="Abercrombie", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=28.1, y=31.5},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={101}, names={"The Totem of Infliction"}, text="Finish Madame Eva's list. The 10 Ghoul Fangs drop from the ghouls at the east edge of Raven Hill Cemetery, south-west of the shack: Flesh Eaters (24-25) and Rotted Ones (25-26). They are well above you: pull single ghouls out to the edge, Stoneclaw Totem first, Earth Shock on cooldown, heal early, and do not go deeper in, where Plague Spreaders and Brain Eaters (27-29) wait. Stoneform removes their disease. Skeleton Fingers also drop from Skeletal Horrors (23-24) around Raven Hill, the venom from any spider. If the fangs are too hard at your level, leave the list open: the route is back here in segment 10.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=23.8, y=37.1},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={230}, names={"Sven's Camp"}, text="Back to Sven Yorgen at his camp", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=7.8, y=34.1},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={262}, names={"The Shadowy Figure"}, text="Sven Yorgen", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=7.8, y=34.1},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={226}, names={"Wolves at Our Heels"}, text="Lars", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=7.7, y=33.2},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={96139}, names={"The Valor Family"}, text="Follow the road east across the whole zone to Darkshire (Ghost Wolf). Sirra Von'Indi in the town hall.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.6, y=47.5, path={{8.3,31.3},{13.1,29.8},{16.3,26.8},{28.4,30.1},{32.2,35.8},{32.6,53.4},{36.8,59.4},{40.0,60.6},{49.4,60.9},{63.0,58.8},{64.0,55.5},{68.0,49.9},{68.8,45.7}}},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={56}, names={"The Night Watch"}, text="Commander Althea Ebonlocke", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.5, y=46.8},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={57}, names={"The Night Watch"}, text="Commander Althea Ebonlocke. Level 24-25 skeletons at Raven Hill: kept for segment 10.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.5, y=46.8},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={148,262}, names={"Supplies from Darkshire","The Shadowy Figure"}, text="Madame Eva", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=45.3},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={149,265}, names={"Ghost Hair Thread","The Shadowy Search Continues"}, text="Madame Eva", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=45.3},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={101}, names={"The Totem of Infliction"}, text="Madame Eva, if you have 10 fangs, 10 fingers and 5 venom vials. If not, press Skip and hand it in on the next Duskwood trip.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=45.3},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={5}, names={"Jitters' Growling Gut"}, text="Chef Grual in the tavern", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.8, y=43.5},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={93}, names={"Dusky Crab Cakes"}, text="Chef Grual", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.8, y=43.5},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={93}, names={"Dusky Crab Cakes"}, text="6 Gooey Spider Legs. You should have them from the spiders on the south road; if not, more spiders sit beside the road west of town.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=30.4, y=50.2, path={{71.8,46.6},{68.8,45.7},{68.0,49.9},{64.0,55.5},{63.8,57.6},{59.4,59.7},{50.6,60.0},{49.2,61.2},{40.0,60.6},{36.8,59.4}}},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={93}, names={"Dusky Crab Cakes"}, text="Chef Grual", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.8, y=43.5, path={{36.8,59.4},{40.0,60.6},{49.2,61.2},{50.6,60.0},{59.4,59.7},{63.0,58.8},{64.0,55.5},{68.0,49.9},{68.8,45.7},{71.8,46.6}}},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={240}, names={"Return to Jitters"}, text="Chef Grual. The crab cakes go back to Jitters in segment 10.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.8, y=43.5},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={265}, names={"The Shadowy Search Continues"}, text="Clerk Daltry in the town hall", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.5, y=46.9},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={266}, names={"Inquire at the Inn"}, text="Clerk Daltry", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.5, y=46.9},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={266}, names={"Inquire at the Inn"}, text="Tavernkeep Smitts in the tavern", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.8, y=44.5},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={453}, names={"Finding the Shadowy Figure"}, text="Tavernkeep Smitts. Keep it for segment 10.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.8, y=44.5},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={149}, names={"Ghost Hair Thread"}, text="Blind Mary, in the house south of town", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=82.0, y=59.1},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={154}, names={"Return the Comb"}, text="Blind Mary", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=82.0, y=59.1},
  {t="C", seg=6, q={177}, names={"Look To The Stars"}, text="Press Skip if you never had a Bronze Tube. The Insane Ghoul (26) stands in the chapel of Tranquil Gardens Cemetery (80.9, 72.0). Kill the skeletons near the chapel first so the fight stays one on one. He is four levels above you and your shocks will often be resisted: start at full health and mana, Stoneclaw Totem at once, Earth Shock when ready, Healing Wave before you drop below half. He drops Mary's Looking Glass.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=80.9, y=72.0},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={154}, names={"Return the Comb"}, text="Back in Darkshire: Madame Eva", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=45.3},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={157}, names={"Deliver the Thread"}, text="Madame Eva. The thread goes to Abercrombie in segment 10.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=45.3},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={177}, names={"Look To The Stars"}, text="Viktori Prism'Antras", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=79.8, y=48.0},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={181}, names={"Look To The Stars"}, text="Viktori Prism'Antras. The ogre Zzarc'Vul is level 33: kept for segment 10.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=79.8, y=48.0},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={66}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Madame Eva: The Legend of Stalvan (needs level 22)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=75.8, y=45.3},
  {t="T", seg=6, q={66}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Clerk Daltry in the town hall", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.5, y=46.9},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={67}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Clerk Daltry. It sends you to Moonbrook in Westfall: kept for segment 10.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=72.5, y=46.9},
  {t="A", seg=6, q={377}, names={"Crime and Punishment"}, text="Councilman Millstipe in Darkshire. The hand of Dextren Ward.", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=71.9, y=47.8, dg=3},
  {t="H", seg=6, arg="Thelsamar", text="Hearthstone to Thelsamar. Next stop: the Wetlands."},
  {t="C", seg=7, q={455}, names={"The Algaz Gauntlet"}, text="From Thelsamar run the road north (Ghost Wolf), past the northern guard tower and Mountaineer Rockgar, into the Dun Algaz tunnels. Finish what is still missing of 8 Dragonmaw Scouts (19-20) and 6 Dragonmaw Grunts (20-21) along the road and in the camps beside it, and walk the road all the way through to the Wetlands side.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=48.6, y=77.0},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={94499}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Where the road leaves the hills, turn east along the foot of the southern cliffs to the waterfalls. Hervdana Saegrund is in her cave beneath the falls.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=65.7, y=76.4},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={94500}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Hervdana Saegrund. The Unfilled Blue Waterskin is filled in the lake around Astranaar in Ashenvale: that is the next segment.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=65.7, y=76.4},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={276}, names={"Tramping Paws"}, text="Go back to the road and follow it north (Ghost Wolf) to the Green Belt. Rethiel the Greenwarden stands in the trees east of the road (56.4, 40.4).", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=56.4, y=40.4, path={{67.0,79.2},{68.8,75.6},{68.8,70.2},{65.6,66.3},{65.6,54.0},{66.4,50.4},{59.6,43.3},{57.0,43.3},{56.0,41.8}}},
  {t="C", seg=7, q={276}, names={"Tramping Paws"}, text="His gnolls are the ones you just passed: Mosshide Gnolls (20-21) and Mosshide Mongrels (21-22) fill the marsh in the south-east, between the Dun Algaz road and Hervdana's falls (54-67, 56-76). Go back south and kill 15 Gnolls and 10 Mongrels. They stand in small groups: pull with a shock from far away, Earthbind Totem for runners, Stoneclaw Totem when a third joins.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=61.0, y=68.0, path={{56.0,41.8},{57.0,43.3},{59.6,43.3},{66.4,50.4},{65.0,63.9},{64.0,65.4},{60.8,66.0}}},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={276}, names={"Tramping Paws"}, text="Rethiel the Greenwarden", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=56.4, y=40.4, path={{60.8,66.0},{64.0,65.4},{65.0,63.9},{66.4,50.4},{59.6,43.3},{57.0,43.3},{56.0,41.8}}},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={277}, names={"Fire Taboo"}, text="Rethiel the Greenwarden", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=56.4, y=40.4},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={469}, names={"Daily Delivery"}, text="Einar Stonegrip, the crocolisk hunter camped a little west of Rethiel, by the road (49.9, 39.4)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=49.9, y=39.4},
  {t="C", seg=7, q={277}, names={"Fire Taboo"}, text="9 Crude Flints. Mosshide Fenrunners (22-23) carry them: they roam all around the Green Belt, on both sides of the road here. Mistweavers (22-23) drop them too: Earth Shock their casts. Black Oozes crawl around in the same marsh; they matter later, not now.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=51.0, y=40.0},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={277}, names={"Fire Taboo"}, text="Rethiel the Greenwarden", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=56.4, y=40.4},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={275}, names={"Blisters on The Land"}, text="Rethiel the Greenwarden. Fen Creepers are level 24-25 and hide in the waterways further north and west: kill the ones you happen to meet, and keep the quest for segment 9.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=56.4, y=40.4},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={294}, names={"Ormer's Revenge"}, text="Follow the road west, then leave it to the south for Whelgar's Excavation Site. Ormer Ironbraid stands at its entrance (38.2, 50.9). Needs level 22. Do not go down into the dig: the raptors there are 25-27.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=38.2, y=50.9},
  {t="C", seg=7, q={294}, names={"Ormer's Revenge"}, text="The raptors he wants live west of the dig, on both sides of the road to Menethil Harbor: kill 10 Mottled Raptors (22-23) and 10 Mottled Screechers (24-25). Screechers call for help, so fight them away from other raptors and use Earthbind Totem. You hand this in when the big loop brings you back to Ormer.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=25.5, y=49.5},
  {t="F", seg=7, arg="Menethil Harbor", text="Keep west on the road to its end and cross the bridge into Menethil Harbor. Shellei Brondir, the gryphon master, stands by the docks.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.5, y=59.7},
  {t="S", seg=7, arg="Menethil Harbor", text="Innkeeper Helbrek in the Deepwater Tavern", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.7, y=61.0},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={455}, names={"The Algaz Gauntlet"}, text="Valstag Ironjaw, outside the keep in the middle of town", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.1, y=56.9},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={98197}, names={"Spoils of War"}, text="Valstag Ironjaw: Spoils of War (new in Forever)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.2, y=56.8},
  {t="C", seg=7, q={98197}, names={"Spoils of War"}, text="Recover 6 Khaz Modan Timber and 30 Khaz Modan Iron from Menethil Harbor. The quest says they lie under water in the harbor; the data has no exact spots. Dive around the docks and piers and look for timber and iron you can click. Come up for air in time.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.1, y=56.9},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={98197}, names={"Spoils of War"}, text="Valstag Ironjaw", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.0, y=56.8},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={469}, names={"Daily Delivery"}, text="James Halloran, the tanner on the north-west side of town", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.5, y=55.7},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={484}, names={"Young Crocolisk Skins"}, text="James Halloran", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.6, y=55.7},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={279}, names={"Claws from the Deep"}, text="Karl Boran, by the docks", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.3, y=58.6},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={98282}, names={"Alchemical Hazards"}, text="Caitlin Grassman: Alchemical Hazards (new in Forever)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=11.9, y=58.8},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={470}, names={"Digging Through the Ooze"}, text="Sida, next to her", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=11.8, y=58.0},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={305}, names={"In Search of The Excavation Team"}, text="Tarrel Rockweaver, on the north side of town (needs level 21)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=11.5, y=52.2},
  {t="C", seg=7, q={279}, names={"Claws from the Deep"}, text="Leave by the bridge and go north along the coast. The Bluegill camp is at the river mouth (15.5, 40.1): kill 12 Bluegill Murlocs (20-21). Gobbler (22) walks at the east end of the camp (18.1, 39.8): loot his head. Other Bluegill types do not count for the 12 but come along if you pull carelessly: Earthbind Totem, and fight at the edge of the camp.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=15.5, y=40.1},
  {t="C", seg=7, q={484}, names={"Young Crocolisk Skins"}, text="Follow the river east. Young Wetlands Crocolisks (21-22) lie on its banks and in every waterway of the marsh: 4 skins. Leave the Wetlands Crocolisks (23-24) and Giant ones alone unless they come for you.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=30.0, y=40.0},
  {t="C", seg=7, q={470}, names={"Digging Through the Ooze"}, text="Sida's Bag is inside an ooze. Kill every Black Ooze (23-24) you pass while you cross the marsh: they can carry it. If you still have no bag, go to Ironbeard's Tomb in the north (44.4, 24.8), where the Crimson Oozes (24-25) sit close together, and kill oozes there until it drops. Oozes hit slowly: melee them and save mana.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=44.4, y=24.8},
  {t="C", seg=7, q={98282}, names={"Alchemical Hazards"}, text="Cross to the south-east. Thelgen Rock is the spider cave in the cliffs south of the Green Belt (around 50, 62). Kill Leech Stalkers and Cave Stalkers (21-22) inside and in front of the cave until one drops an Unruptured Stalker Gland. Stoneform removes their poison. Leave the Leech Widow (24 elite) deeper inside alone.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=50.3, y=61.9, path={{52.9,62.9}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={305}, names={"In Search of The Excavation Team"}, text="Back north-west to Whelgar's Excavation Site. Merrin Rockweaver stands near Ormer at the entrance (38.9, 52.3).", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=38.9, y=52.3},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={306}, names={"In Search of The Excavation Team"}, text="Merrin Rockweaver", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=38.9, y=52.3},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={294}, names={"Ormer's Revenge"}, text="Ormer Ironbraid", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=38.2, y=50.9},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={295}, names={"Ormer's Revenge"}, text="Ormer Ironbraid. Scytheclaws and Razormaws are 25-27: kept for segment 9.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=38.2, y=50.9},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={306}, names={"In Search of The Excavation Team"}, text="Take the road back to Menethil Harbor. Tarrel Rockweaver, on the north side of town.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=11.5, y=52.2},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={484}, names={"Young Crocolisk Skins"}, text="James Halloran", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.6, y=55.7},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={471}, names={"Apprentice's Duties"}, text="James Halloran. Giant Crocolisks are 25-26: kept for segment 9.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.6, y=55.7},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={279}, names={"Claws from the Deep"}, text="Karl Boran", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.3, y=58.6},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={281}, names={"Reclaiming Goods"}, text="Karl Boran", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.3, y=58.6},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={98282}, names={"Alchemical Hazards"}, text="Caitlin Grassman", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=11.9, y=58.8},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={470}, names={"Digging Through the Ooze"}, text="Sida", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=11.8, y=58.0},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={281}, names={"Reclaiming Goods"}, text="Back to the Bluegill camps on the coast north of town. Click the Damaged Crate (13.5, 41.4).", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=13.5, y=41.4},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={284}, names={"The Search Continues"}, text="From the Damaged Crate", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=13.5, y=41.4},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={284}, names={"The Search Continues"}, text="The Sealed Barrel, a little further north (13.6, 38.2)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=13.6, y=38.2},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={285}, names={"Search More Hovels"}, text="From the Sealed Barrel", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=13.6, y=38.2},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={285}, names={"Search More Hovels"}, text="The Half-buried Barrel in the northern camp (13.9, 34.8). Murlocs stand right next to each container: clear them first, a click is interrupted when you are hit.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=13.9, y=34.8},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={286}, names={"Return the Statuette"}, text="From the Half-buried Barrel", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=13.9, y=34.8},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={286}, names={"Return the Statuette"}, text="Karl Boran, by the Menethil docks", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.3, y=58.6},
  {t="A", seg=7, q={98189}, names={"Return the Statuette"}, text="Karl Boran: Return the Statuette (new in Forever)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.4, y=58.5},
  {t="T", seg=7, q={98189}, names={"Return the Statuette"}, text="Captain Stoutfist, inside Menethil Keep. Do not take his other quests yet: they belong to segment 9.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.9, y=57.4},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=7, text="Optional, about 10 minutes: fly from Menethil Harbor to Ironforge, learn your level 24 spells from Eldrun Stormbreaker (47.6, 13.5) and fly back. No shaman trainer is known in Kalimdor, so the next chance is at level 28. Press Skip if you would rather go on."},
  {t="N", seg=7, arg="Take the boat from Menethil Harbor to Auberdine", text="Buy food and water first. Not verified for Forever: Hervdana's quest text says the Auberdine boat stops in Southshore on the way over. If it does, stay on board until Auberdine in Darkshore."},
  {t="F", seg=8, arg="Auberdine", text="Walk off the dock into Auberdine. Caylais Moonfeather, the hippogryph master, stands at the foot of the dock.", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=36.3, y=45.6},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={97894}, names={"Business in Auberdine"}, text="Gorbold Steelhand, at a merchant stall in Auberdine: the message from his brother in Stormwind", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=38.1, y=41.2},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={729}, names={"The Absent Minded Prospector"}, text="Archaeologist Hollee, the dwarf in the north part of the village", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=37.4, y=41.8},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={965}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze, in the building on the east side of the village", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=39.0, y=43.6},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={965}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Follow the road north out of Auberdine (Ghost Wolf) and turn east where the land rises toward the Tower of Althalaxx. Balthule Shadowstrike hides below the tower (55.0, 24.9).", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=55.0, y=24.9},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={966}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Balthule Shadowstrike", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=55.0, y=24.9},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={966}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Dark Strand Fanatics (16-17) camp around the tower: kill them for 4 Worn Parchments. They are far below you. Do not climb the tower: Athrikus Narassin (31) is at the top.", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=56.3, y=26.7},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={966}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Balthule Shadowstrike", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=55.0, y=24.9},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={967}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Balthule Shadowstrike. A letter for Maestra's Post in Ashenvale.", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=55.0, y=24.9},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={729}, names={"The Absent Minded Prospector"}, text="Run back past Auberdine and take the road south (Ghost Wolf), a long way. Near the south end of Darkshore leave the road to the west: Prospector Remtravel stands in his dig (35.7, 83.7). Do not take his escort (elite).", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=35.7, y=83.7, path={{52.4,28.3},{49.2,28.3},{48.0,30.1},{47.6,39.7},{44.2,42.7},{43.6,49.6},{39.6,53.7},{38.8,58.8},{39.0,69.6},{38.2,71.1},{38.4,80.4}}},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={945}, names={"Therylune's Escape"}, text="Therylune is in the Master's Glaive, the ruin just south-east of the dig (38.6, 87.3). Kill the cultists around her first.", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=38.6, y=87.3},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={945}, names={"Therylune's Escape"}, text="Escort: walk with Therylune until she is out of the Master's Glaive. Stay ahead of her and kill what attacks; everything here is far below you.", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=38.6, y=87.3},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={5321}, names={"The Sleeper Has Awakened"}, text="Go north-east to the Grove of the Ancients, beside the road (44.4, 76.4). Kerlonian Evershade sleeps there.", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=44.4, y=76.4},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={5321}, names={"The Sleeper Has Awakened"}, text="Take the Horn of Awakening out of Kerlonian's Chest next to him, then escort Kerlonian south along the road. He follows you and keeps falling asleep: use the Horn of Awakening on him each time. Stay on the road and walk (no Ghost Wolf, he cannot keep up). Changed in Forever: the objective now reads \"escort Kerlonian on the road south to his bag\", still in Darkshore, so the escort part may end before Ashenvale. The hand-in is still listed at Maestra's Post.", zone="Darkshore", map=1439, x=40.9, y=85.9},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={5321}, names={"The Sleeper Has Awakened"}, text="Maestra's Post is the first camp on the road inside Ashenvale. Liladris Moonriver stands at its north end (27.3, 35.6).", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=27.3, y=35.6},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={967}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Delgren the Purifier, in the camp (26.2, 38.7)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=26.2, y=38.7},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={970}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Delgren the Purifier", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=26.2, y=38.7},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1010}, names={"Bathran's Hair"}, text="Orendil Broadleaf, next to him", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=26.4, y=38.6},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={970}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="The Dark Strand cultists dig in the ruins north-east of Maestra's Post (around 31, 31). Kill Cultists, Adepts, Excavators (18-20) and the Enforcer until one drops the Glowing Soul Gem.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=31.3, y=30.8},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1010}, names={"Bathran's Hair"}, text="Bathran's Haunt is further north (around 32, 23). Pick 5 Bathran's Hair from the Plant Bundles on the ground between the Forsaken there (18-20).", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=31.7, y=23.0},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1010}, names={"Bathran's Hair"}, text="Back at Maestra's Post: Orendil Broadleaf", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=26.4, y=38.6},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1020}, names={"Orendil's Cure"}, text="Orendil Broadleaf. His cure goes to Astranaar.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=26.4, y=38.6},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={970}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Delgren the Purifier", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=26.2, y=38.7},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={973}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Delgren the Purifier", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=26.2, y=38.7},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={945}, names={"Therylune's Escape"}, text="Go south from Maestra's Post, across the road. Therysil stands at the Shrine of Aessina (22.6, 51.9).", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=22.6, y=51.9},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={973}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Fire Scar Shrine is just south of the Shrine of Aessina. Ilkrud Magthrull (24) stands in the middle of it (25.3, 60.7) with Felslayers (22-23) all around. Clear a path of Felslayers one at a time (they drain mana: kill them fast), then fight Ilkrud with full mana: Earth Shock his Shadow Bolts and drop Stoneclaw Totem for whatever he calls. He drops Ilkrud Magthrull's Tome. You hand it in when you pass Maestra's Post again.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=25.3, y=60.7},
  {t="F", seg=8, arg="Astranaar", text="Go back north to the road and follow it east to Astranaar, the town on the island in the lake. Daelyshia, the hippogryph master, stands at the west entrance.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=34.4, y=48.0},
  {t="S", seg=8, arg="Astranaar", text="Innkeeper Kimlya in the inn", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=37.0, y=49.2},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1008}, names={"The Zoram Strand"}, text="Shindrell Swiftfire, near the west entrance", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=34.7, y=48.8},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={991}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Raene Wolfrunner, in the building in the middle of town", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=36.6, y=49.6},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1020}, names={"Orendil's Cure"}, text="Pelturas Whitemoon, in the house at the south-east end of town", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=37.4, y=51.8},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1033}, names={"Elune's Tear"}, text="Pelturas Whitemoon", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=37.4, y=51.8},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={94500}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Call of Water: walk down to the lake that surrounds Astranaar and use the Unfilled Blue Waterskin at the water. The quest only says \"the waters of Astranaar\"; any spot on the shore next to town should do. Keep the Full Blue Waterskin: it goes back to Hervdana in the Wetlands in segment 9.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=34.4, y=48.0},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={991}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Take the road west out of Astranaar and leave it to the north-west for Lake Falathim. Teronis' Corpse lies at the lake (20.3, 42.3).", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=20.3, y=42.3},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1023}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="From Teronis' Corpse", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=20.3, y=42.3},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1023}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Saltspittle murlocs (19-21) around the lake: kill them until one drops the Glowing Gem.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=20.4, y=42.7},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1007}, names={"The Ancient Statuette"}, text="Keep north-west to the coast. Talen camps above the Zoram Strand (14.8, 31.3). The Horde has a camp on the shore south-west of him (Classic knowledge, not checked for Forever): stay away from its guards.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=14.8, y=31.3},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1007}, names={"The Ancient Statuette"}, text="The Ancient Statuette lies on the strand north of Talen (14.2, 20.6). Fight your way there through the Wrathtail naga and count their heads.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=14.2, y=20.6},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1007}, names={"The Ancient Statuette"}, text="Talen", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=14.8, y=31.3},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1009}, names={"Ruuzel"}, text="Talen", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=14.8, y=31.3},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1009,1008}, names={"Ruuzel","The Zoram Strand"}, text="Kill naga along the strand until you have 20 Wrathtail Heads: Wave Riders and Sorceresses (18-19) on the near side, Razortails and Sea Witches (19-20) further out, Myrmidons and Priestesses (20-21) at the north end. Ruuzel (22) stands with her guards on the small island at the north end (7.2, 13.1): pull the guards one at a time with a shock from maximum range, then kill her for the Ring of Zoram. Earth Shock the casters' heals and lightning. Lady Vespia, a rare elite who walks the strand, also carries the ring: leave her unless she is alone and you are at full health.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=9.0, y=18.0},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1009}, names={"Ruuzel"}, text="Talen", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=14.8, y=31.3},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={973}, names={"The Tower of Althalaxx"}, text="Walk back east to Maestra's Post: Delgren the Purifier", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=26.2, y=38.7},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={976}, names={"Supplies to Auberdine"}, text="Feero Ironhand, standing next to Delgren. This starts an escort with three ambushes.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=26.2, y=38.9},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={976}, names={"Supplies to Auberdine"}, text="Walk with Feero. Three groups attack one after the other, the last one the strongest. Eat and drink to full before you talk to him, drop Stoneclaw Totem at the start of each ambush, kill the casters first with Earth Shock on their casts, and heal between waves. Feero fights too, but he must survive.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=26.2, y=38.9},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={976}, names={"Supplies to Auberdine"}, text="Delgren the Purifier at Maestra's Post", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=26.2, y=38.7},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1008}, names={"The Zoram Strand"}, text="Back along the road to Astranaar: Shindrell Swiftfire", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=34.7, y=48.8},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1134}, names={"Pridewings of Stonetalon"}, text="Shindrell Swiftfire. The wyverns are in Stonetalon, later in this segment.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=34.7, y=48.8},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1023}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Raene Wolfrunner", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=36.6, y=49.6},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1024,1025,1054}, names={"Raene's Cleansing","An Aggressive Defense","Culling the Threat"}, text="Raene Wolfrunner", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=36.6, y=49.6},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1070}, names={"On Guard in Stonetalon"}, text="Sentinel Thenysil, on the west side of town", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=34.9, y=49.8},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1056}, names={"Journey to Stonetalon Peak"}, text="Faldreas Goeth'Shael, near Raene's building", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=35.8, y=49.1},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1054}, names={"Culling the Threat"}, text="Thistlefur Village is in the hills north of Astranaar. Dal Bloodclaw (25) stands at 37.7, 34.7 among Thistlefur furbolgs (23-24), many of them Shamans who heal. Pull single furbolgs on the way in, Earth Shock every heal, and take Dal with full mana and Stoneclaw Totem down. Loot his skull.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=37.7, y=34.7},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1033}, names={"Elune's Tear"}, text="Come back down to the road and follow it east to Iris Lake, north of the road. Elune's Tear lies on the small island in the lake (46.4, 46.4): pick one up.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=46.4, y=46.4},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1024}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Shael'dryn stands at the moonwell further east, north of the road (53.5, 46.2)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=53.5, y=46.2},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1026}, names={"Raene's Cleansing"}, text="Shael'dryn. Keep this one: the rod pieces are for the second Ashenvale trip (segment 12).", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=53.5, y=46.2},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1054}, names={"Culling the Threat"}, text="Back to Astranaar: Raene Wolfrunner", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=36.6, y=49.6, path={{52.6,50.7},{49.8,51.6},{48.2,54.0},{44.8,54.0},{43.2,48.4},{36.8,48.1}}},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1033}, names={"Elune's Tear"}, text="Pelturas Whitemoon", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=37.4, y=51.8},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1034}, names={"The Ruins of Stardust"}, text="Pelturas Whitemoon", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=37.4, y=51.8},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1034}, names={"The Ruins of Stardust"}, text="Leave Astranaar and go south. The Ruins of Stardust are on the island in the lake south of town (33.3, 67.8): pick 5 Handfuls of Stardust from the Stardust Covered Bushes.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=33.3, y=67.8},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1016}, names={"Elemental Bracers"}, text="Go east along the south side of the zone, past the mouth of the Talondeep Path, to Silverwind Refuge on the shore of Mystral Lake. Sentinel Velene Starstrike is there (49.8, 67.2).", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=49.8, y=67.2},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1016}, names={"Elemental Bracers"}, text="Befouled Water Elementals (23-25) walk in and around Mystral Lake. Kill them for 5 Intact Elemental Bracers, then right-click the Divining Scroll she gave you to make the Divined Scroll.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=49.0, y=70.4},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1016}, names={"Elemental Bracers"}, text="Sentinel Velene Starstrike", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=49.8, y=67.2},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1017}, names={"Mage Summoner"}, text="Sentinel Velene Starstrike", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=49.8, y=67.2},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1025}, names={"An Aggressive Defense"}, text="The Foulweald furbolgs live in Greenpaw Village, north-east of Silverwind Refuge (49-58, 60-65). Kill 1 Den Watcher, 2 Ursas (both 24-25, in the middle of the village), 10 Totemics and 12 Warriors (23-24). Earth Shock the Totemics before they heal, kill their totems, and pull from the edge so you fight two at most.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=53.3, y=62.0},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1017}, names={"Mage Summoner"}, text="Sarilus Foulborne (25) stands on the island in the middle of Mystral Lake. Clear the elementals near the island, then fight him with full mana: Earth Shock his casts, and drop Stoneclaw Totem if he has a summoned servant with him. Loot his head. (Questie files him under a Barrens map position; the lake is where the quest sends you.)", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=49.0, y=70.4},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1017}, names={"Mage Summoner"}, text="Sentinel Velene Starstrike", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=49.8, y=67.2},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={98027}, names={"Gleaming Crescent Necklace"}, text="Only if you are level 25, otherwise press Skip here and on its hand-in. A Gleaming Crescent Pendant lies on the ground east of Mystral Lake (63.0, 71.5): clicking it starts a level 29 quest (new in Forever). The woods out there are above your level: go in Ghost Wolf, take the pendant and leave.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=63.0, y=71.5, path={{48.4,65.7},{49.2,63.9},{57.2,64.2},{58.6,66.3},{59.4,70.8},{60.4,72.0}}},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1070}, names={"On Guard in Stonetalon"}, text="Go back west to the Talondeep Path, the tunnel in the southern cliffs (entrance at Ashenvale 42.3, 71.0), and run through it into the Stonetalon Mountains. You come out in Windshear Crag. Kaela Shadowspear watches the valley from its south-west side (59.9, 66.8).", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=59.9, y=66.8},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1085}, names={"On Guard in Stonetalon"}, text="Kaela Shadowspear", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=59.9, y=66.8},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1085}, names={"On Guard in Stonetalon"}, text="Gaxim Rustfizzle, a few steps from her", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=59.5, y=67.1},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1071}, names={"A Gnome's Respite"}, text="Gaxim Rustfizzle", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=59.5, y=67.2},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1093}, names={"Super Reaper 6000"}, text="Ziz Fizziks, in the small hut a little north (59.0, 62.6)", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=59, y=62.6},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1071,1093}, names={"A Gnome's Respite","Super Reaper 6000"}, text="The Venture Co. camps fill Windshear Crag north-east of here. Kill 10 Loggers (18-19) and 10 Deforesters (19-20), and Operators (19-20, around the machines) until one drops the Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints.", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=65.9, y=52.6},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1090}, names={"Gerenzo's Orders"}, text="Piznik stands at the back of the Windshear Mine, the kobold mine in the south-east wall of the crag (71.9, 60.0). Kill the Windshear kobolds (20-22) on the way in.", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=71.9, y=60.0, path={{74.1,59.6}}, cave=true},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={1090}, names={"Gerenzo's Orders"}, text="Piznik starts mining and kobolds attack in waves until he is done. Stand at the tunnel in front of him, drop Stoneclaw Totem when a wave arrives and Earthbind Totem to keep them together, and heal between waves. He must survive.", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=71.9, y=60.0, path={{74.1,59.6}}, cave=true},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1090}, names={"Gerenzo's Orders"}, text="Piznik", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=71.9, y=60.0},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={1092}, names={"Gerenzo's Orders"}, text="Piznik", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=71.9, y=60.0},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1092,1093}, names={"Gerenzo's Orders","Super Reaper 6000"}, text="Ziz Fizziks. Do not take Further Instructions (it sends you to Ratchet).", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=59.0, y=62.6, path={{69.4,58.2},{64.2,58.2},{61.2,62.7}}},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1071}, names={"A Gnome's Respite"}, text="Gaxim Rustfizzle. Do not take An Old Colleague (it sends you to Ironforge and Stormwind).", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=59.5, y=67.2},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={86574}, names={"Stonetalon Supply Run"}, text="Follow the road west and then north through the mountains to Mirkfallon Lake. On the way it passes below Sun Rock Retreat, a Horde town (Classic knowledge): stay on the road in Ghost Wolf and do not go up the side path. The body of the Night Elf Courier lies at the lake (48.6, 39.8): Stonetalon Supply Run (new in Forever).", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=48.6, y=39.8},
  {t="C", seg=8, q={86574,1134}, names={"Stonetalon Supply Run","Pridewings of Stonetalon"}, text="Pridewing wyverns fly all around Mirkfallon Lake: Wyverns (21-22), Consorts (22-23) and Skyhunters (23-24). Kill them for 12 Pridewing Venom Sacs and 6 Stonetalon Supply Bundles (the new quest's bundles come from the same wyverns). Stoneform removes their poison. Leave the Pridewing Patriarch (25, rare elite) alone.", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=50.6, y=43.0},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={86574}, names={"Stonetalon Supply Run"}, text="Take the road north from the lake up to Stonetalon Peak. Innkeeper Faralia is in the inn (35.7, 5.8).", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=35.7, y=5.8, path={{51.8,42.4},{51.8,39.1},{50.0,34.0},{50.0,30.4},{49.0,28.9},{45.2,28.0},{44.0,25.9},{43.2,15.1},{41.6,12.7},{39.4,12.1},{39.4,8.2},{37.8,5.8}}},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1056}, names={"Journey to Stonetalon Peak"}, text="Keeper Albagorm, the big Keeper of the Grove on the hill (37.1, 8.1). Do not take his follow-up.", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=37.1, y=8.1},
  {t="F", seg=8, arg="Stonetalon Peak", text="Teloren, the hippogryph master", zone="Stonetalon Mountains", map=1442, x=36.4, y=7.2},
  {t="FLY", seg=8, arg="Astranaar", text="Teloren. If the flight is not offered, use your hearthstone: it is bound in Astranaar."},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1134}, names={"Pridewings of Stonetalon"}, text="Shindrell Swiftfire", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=34.7, y=48.8},
  {t="A", seg=8, q={95737}, names={"Seeking Caitlin"}, text="Llana in Astranaar. It only sends you to Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=34.9, y=48.5, dg=5},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1025}, names={"An Aggressive Defense"}, text="Raene Wolfrunner", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=36.6, y=49.6},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={1034}, names={"The Ruins of Stardust"}, text="Pelturas Whitemoon", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=37.4, y=51.8},
  {t="T", seg=8, q={98027}, names={"Gleaming Crescent Necklace"}, text="Maliynn, in the building next to Raene (36.6, 49.9). Press Skip if you never picked up the pendant.", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=36.6, y=49.9},
  {t="N", seg=8, arg="Optional dungeon: Blackfathom Deeps, levels 24-32", text="The entrance is on the north-west coast of Ashenvale, north of the Zoram Strand: go down through the ruins and the tunnels to the portal. Inside: Argent Guard Thaelrid ends In Search of Thaelrid and gives Blackfathom Villainy (the head of Twilight Lord Kelris, for Dawnwatcher Selgorm in Darnassus). Quests you picked up for it: Knowledge in the Deeps. Not on your path, only if you want the detour: Twilight Falls (Darnassus 55, 24); In Search of Thaelrid (Darnassus 55, 25). Needs an earlier quest chain this route does not do: Researching the Corruption. The route does not come back to these hand-ins, go when it suits you: Blackfathom Villainy (Darnassus).", zone="Ashenvale", map=1440, x=14.5, y=14.2, dg=4, run=true},
  {t="FLY", seg=8, arg="Auberdine", text="Daelyshia, at the west entrance of Astranaar"},
  {t="N", seg=8, arg="Take the boat from Auberdine to Menethil Harbor", text="Check on the dock which boat it is: one pier goes to Menethil Harbor, the other to Darnassus. The Full Blue Waterskin and Raene's Cleansing stay in your log."},
  {t="S", seg=9, arg="Menethil Harbor", text="You step off the boat from Auberdine. Bind at the Deepwater Tavern (Innkeeper Helbrek): you hearth back here after the first loop", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.7, y=60.9},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={473}, names={"Report to Captain Stoutfist"}, text="Valstag Ironjaw, in front of Menethil Keep (10.1,56.9)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.1, y=56.9},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={473}, names={"Report to Captain Stoutfist"}, text="Captain Stoutfist, inside Menethil Keep", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.9, y=57.5},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={464}, names={"War Banners"}, text="Captain Stoutfist", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.9, y=57.5},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={98221}, names={"From the Ashes"}, text="Captain Stoutfist (new in Forever)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.9, y=57.4},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={98230}, names={"This Land Was Their Land"}, text="Captain Stoutfist (new in Forever): a walk to Howin Kindfeather, far east along the road", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.9, y=57.4},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={98190}, names={"A Friend of the Family"}, text="Captain Stoutfist (new in Forever). The Menethil Statuette goes to Stormwind Keep in the next segment: keep it in your bags", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.9, y=57.4},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={472}, names={"Fall of Dun Modr"}, text="Harlo Barnaby (10.8,55.9). Needs level 25. Just a walk to Dun Modr: you hand it in in segment 11", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.8, y=55.9},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={98208}, names={"Bloom of the Heavens"}, text="Sylessa Duskwhisper (new in Forever), near the tanner. Her flower is in the wreck south of town: you get it after the first loop", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.0, y=55.9},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={288}, names={"The Third Fleet"}, text="First Mate Fitzsimmons, by the docks", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.9, y=59.6},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={288}, names={"The Third Fleet"}, text="Buy a Flagon of Mead from Innkeeper Helbrek in the Deepwater Tavern", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.7, y=60.9},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={288}, names={"The Third Fleet"}, text="First Mate Fitzsimmons", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.9, y=59.6},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={289}, names={"The Cursed Crew"}, text="First Mate Fitzsimmons", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.9, y=59.6},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={471}, names={"Apprentice's Duties"}, text="Leave by the bridge and go north along the coast (Ghost Wolf). Giant Wetlands Crocolisks (25-26) swim in the river mouths at 15-27,19-29, next to the shipwrecks. Kill until you have 6 skins. Fen Creepers (24-25, stealthed in the water at 18-24,27-32) count for Blisters on the Land: kill the ones you meet", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=19.0, y=25.0},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={289}, names={"The Cursed Crew"}, text="The two wrecks on the north coast (13-16,23-31). Cursed Sailors (26-27) are mostly around the southern wreck, Cursed Marines (27-28) around the northern one; First Mate Snellig (29) stands in the southern wreck at 13.8,30.2. They come in twos: Stoneclaw Totem for the second one, Earth Shock when a fight drags, Healing Wave between pulls. Clear around Snellig first, then fight him with full mana", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=14.3, y=26.9},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={471}, names={"Apprentice's Duties"}, text="Walk back to Menethil Harbor. James Halloran, the tanner", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.5, y=55.7},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={98072}, names={"Crocs of the Sky"}, text="James Halloran (new in Forever). The whelps are far to the east; you get them at the end of this loop", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.5, y=55.8},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={289}, names={"The Cursed Crew"}, text="First Mate Fitzsimmons", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.9, y=59.6},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={290}, names={"Lifting the Curse"}, text="First Mate Fitzsimmons", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.9, y=59.6},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={290}, names={"Lifting the Curse"}, text="Back north to the far (northern) wreck. Captain Halyndor (30) stands on it at 15.4,23.6 with Marines around him. Pull the Marines away one at a time first; on Halyndor keep Stoneclaw Totem down, Frost Shock and step back when you need a Healing Wave. He drops the Intrepid Strongbox Key", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=15.4, y=23.6},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={290}, names={"Lifting the Curse"}, text="Intrepid's Locked Strongbox, in the same wreck (14.4,24.0)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=14.4, y=24.0},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={292}, names={"The Eye of Paleth"}, text="The same strongbox", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=14.4, y=24.0},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={299}, names={"Uncovering the Past"}, text="Go south-east across the marsh to Whelgar's Excavation Site (stay north of the road until you are past the murloc coast). Prospector Whelgar stands at the camp on the east rim of the dig (38.8,52.4)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=38.8, y=52.4},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={295,299}, names={"Ormer's Revenge","Uncovering the Past"}, text="Down in the dig (31-36,44-52): kill 10 Mottled Scytheclaws and 10 Mottled Razormaws (25-27) and pick up the four tablet fragments. Ados, Modr and Golm are in Ancient Relics (stone tablets), Neru is in a Loose Soil mound; they sit in different spots each time, so check 34.1,49.9 / 35.2,51.5 / 34.2,47.7 / 33.1,46.4 and the north end around 34.3,44.5 and 36.5,42.1. Raptors pull in pairs: Earthbind Totem and Frost Shock to split them", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=34.0, y=48.0},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={295}, names={"Ormer's Revenge"}, text="Ormer Ironbraid, next to Whelgar", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=38.2, y=50.9},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={296}, names={"Ormer's Revenge"}, text="Ormer Ironbraid", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=38.2, y=50.9},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={296}, names={"Ormer's Revenge"}, text="Sarltooth (29) is at the south-west side of the dig (33.3,51.5). Clear the raptors near him first. Stoneclaw Totem, then Frost Shock and back away while it is slowed; heal early, he hits hard for your level", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=33.3, y=51.5},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={296}, names={"Ormer's Revenge"}, text="Ormer Ironbraid", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=38.2, y=50.9},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={299}, names={"Uncovering the Past"}, text="Prospector Whelgar", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=38.8, y=52.4},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={98221}, obj={1}, names={"From the Ashes"}, text="Go north-east. The first set of Attack Plans lies at the small Dragonmaw post west of the Angerfang Encampment (38.6,46.1). Click it to destroy it. Which of the four plans lies where is not in the data: if this spot is empty, go on and tick it later", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=38.6, y=46.1},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={464,98221}, names={"War Banners","From the Ashes"}, text="Angerfang Encampment (39-52,40-49). Any Dragonmaw drops War Banners (8 needed): Raiders (26-27) and Bonewarders (27, casters: Earth Shock them). The other Attack Plans are at about 45.5,42.6, 45.3,45.5 and 49.4,46.6. Fight at the edges, one tent at a time; the Dragonmaw Battlemaster (rare, 30) walks the middle: avoid him. Leave the catapults for the next loop", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=45.5, y=44.5},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={98230}, names={"This Land Was Their Land"}, text="Howin Kindfeather, just north of the encampment beside the road (49.4,42.1)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=49.4, y=42.1},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={98246}, names={"Trying Times"}, text="Howin Kindfeather (new in Forever). The eggs come from Raptor Ridge in the next loop. If he does not offer it yet, he will after Razormaw Needling in loop B", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=49.4, y=42.1},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={275}, names={"Blisters on The Land"}, text="Finish the 8 Fen Creepers in the water around Rethiel's island (53-55,36-46); they are stealthed until you are close", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=54.5, y=41.0},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={275}, names={"Blisters on The Land"}, text="Rethiel the Greenwarden (56.4,40.4)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=56.4, y=40.4},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={95646}, names={"Horrors in the Highland"}, text="Rethiel the Greenwarden. The root core of a Highland Horror inside.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=56.2, y=40.5, dg=5},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={98072}, names={"Crocs of the Sky"}, text="Crimson Whelps (25-26) fly over the Green Belt east of Rethiel (57-70,31-51). Collect 10 Pristine Crimson Scales. Their fire bolt is a cast: Earth Shock it. Stay north of the orcs in the hills", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=61.0, y=40.0},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={98223}, names={"Old Habits"}, text="Go south-west to the Dragonmaw camp south of the road. The Tattered Spellbook lies on the ground at 53.5,54.5 (new in Forever). Dragonmaw Centurions and Shadowwarders (28-29) stand around it: pull one at a time, Earth Shock the Shadowwarders, and finish your 8 War Banners here if you are short. You keep this quest until segment 11", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=53.5, y=54.5, path={{60.0,49.9},{57.2,54.0}}},
  {t="H", seg=9, arg="Menethil Harbor", text="Hearthstone back to Menethil Harbor"},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={464}, names={"War Banners"}, text="Captain Stoutfist", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.9, y=57.5},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={465}, names={"Nek'rosh's Gambit"}, text="Captain Stoutfist. Do not take Defeat Nek'rosh later: it is an elite fight", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.9, y=57.5},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={98221}, names={"From the Ashes"}, text="Captain Stoutfist. Keep Old Habits (98223) and A Friend of the Family (98190) in the log for later segments", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=9.9, y=57.4},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={98072}, names={"Crocs of the Sky"}, text="James Halloran", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.5, y=55.8},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={98240}, names={"Crimson Crate Delivery"}, text="James Halloran (new in Forever): a crate for Howin Kindfeather", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.5, y=55.8},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={292}, names={"The Eye of Paleth"}, text="Glorin Steelbrow, at the Deepwater Tavern (10.6,60.6)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.6, y=60.6},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={293}, names={"Cleansing the Eye"}, text="Glorin Steelbrow. The eye goes to the Cathedral in Stormwind in the next segment", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=10.6, y=60.6},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={95647}, names={"Lost in the Thicket Things"}, text="Caitlin Grassman in Menethil Harbor. Find out what happened to her husband Ardin inside.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=11.9, y=58.8, dg=5},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={98208}, names={"Bloom of the Heavens"}, text="The wreck just south of town, across the water from the docks (about 12,64). Bluegill Raiders (28-29) live in and around it; kill them and search the wreck for Nord'el. Whether the flower drops or is picked up is not in the data: loot every murloc and click anything that sparkles. Pull one murloc at a time and keep Earthbind Totem down, they run for help", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=12.1, y=64.2},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={98208}, names={"Bloom of the Heavens"}, text="Sylessa Duskwhisper.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.0, y=55.9},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={98209}, names={"Bloom of the Heavens"}, text="Sylessa Duskwhisper: Bloom of the Heavens. Nord'el goes to Auberdine: you carry it until the next boat there", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=8.0, y=55.9},
  {t="N", seg=9, arg="Optional dungeon: Excavation Site: Wetlands, levels 26-31", text="It is in the Wetlands, in the hills above Whelgar's Excavation. Inside: Ardin Grassman's trail leads to Heartwoven (back to Caitlin), the body of a dwarf starts Fallen in the Fen (back to Dorin Songblade in Lakeshire), and the last boss drops a Titan Relic that starts Lost Relic Carry for Prospector Whelgar (Wetlands 38.8, 52.3), who then sends it on to Ironforge. Quests you picked up for it: Seeking Caitlin, Horrors in the Highland, Lost in the Thicket Things. Not on your path, only if you want the detour: Songblade Search (Redridge Mountains 26, 46).", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=47.8, y=56.2, dg=5, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={95809}, names={"Heartwoven"}, text="Heartwoven: Caitlin Grassman.", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=11.9, y=58.8, dg=5},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={98240}, names={"Crimson Crate Delivery"}, text="Follow the road east in Ghost Wolf, past Whelgar's dig, to Howin Kindfeather (49.4,42.1)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=49.4, y=42.1},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={95646}, names={"Horrors in the Highland"}, zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=56.2, y=40.5, dg=5},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={98245}, names={"Razormaw Needling"}, text="Howin Kindfeather (new in Forever). Take Trying Times (98246) too if he only offers it now", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=49.4, y=42.1},
  {t="C", seg=9, q={98245,98246}, names={"Razormaw Needling","Trying Times"}, text="Raptor Ridge, north-east of Howin (58-72,22-40): Highland Razormaws (27-28) and Elder Razormaws (29) drop the 10 Razormaw Incisors and the 12 Perfect Razormaw Eggs (look for nests on the ground too; the data does not say whether the eggs drop or are picked up). Stay at the south and west edge: the Razormaw Matriarch (rare, 31) is deep inside at 70,29. Raptors come in pairs: Stoneclaw Totem, Frost Shock the second one", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=63.0, y=30.5},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={98245}, names={"Razormaw Needling"}, text="Howin Kindfeather", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=49.4, y=42.1},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={98246}, names={"Trying Times"}, text="Howin Kindfeather. Ignore his follow-ups: they are group quests", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=49.4, y=42.1},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={465}, names={"Nek'rosh's Gambit"}, text="Cross the road into the Angerfang Encampment and click a Dragonmaw Catapult (47.5,47.0) to hand in. Do not take Defeat Nek'rosh (elite)", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=47.5, y=47.0},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={94500}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Go south-east to Hervdana Saegrund in her cave at the foot of the southern waterfalls (65.7,76.4), the way you went in segments 5 and 7. Dark Iron dwarves roam near the cave: go around them. She takes the Full Blue Waterskin", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=65.7, y=76.4, path={{56.6,56.4},{57.0,67.8},{60.6,74.1},{62.0,75.9}}},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={94501}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Hervdana Saegrund: the Vial of Purest Water for Norric", zone="Wetlands", map=1437, x=65.7, y=76.4},
  {t="T", seg=9, q={94501}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Take the Dun Algaz road south into Loch Modan (the tunnels start at about 53,70 in the Wetlands). Norric Lochthane is in his house in the north of Loch Modan (41.9,19.0). You receive the Water Sapta", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=41.9, y=19.0},
  {t="A", seg=9, q={94502}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Norric Lochthane. Keep the Water Sapta and the Remaining Drops of Purest Water: Stendel's Pond is in Westfall, next segment", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=41.9, y=19.0},
  {t="FLY", seg=9, arg="Ironforge", text="Run south to Thelsamar and fly to Ironforge (Thorgrum Borrelson)", zone="Loch Modan", map=1432, x=33.9, y=51.0},
  {t="N", seg=9, arg="Segment done. In the log: 57, 67, 157, 181, 240, 453 (Duskwood/Westfall), 293 and 98190 (Stormwind), 472 and 98223 (segment 11), 1026 (Ashenvale), 94502 (Stendel's Pond)", text="Your hearthstone stays in Menethil Harbor"},
  {t="TRAIN", seg=10, text="Ironforge: Eldrun Stormbreaker (47.6, 13.5). Learn your level 26 and 28 spells"},
  {t="N", seg=10, arg="Take the Deeprun Tram from Tinker Town to Stormwind", text="It arrives in the Dwarven District"},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={98190}, names={"A Friend of the Family"}, text="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon in the throne room of Stormwind Keep (new in Forever)", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=80.0, y=38.5},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={98191}, names={"A Friend of the Family"}, text="Highlord Bolvar Fordragon", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=80.0, y=38.5},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={293}, names={"Cleansing the Eye"}, text="Archbishop Benedictus, at the back of the Cathedral of Light", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=50.3, y=45.5},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={98191}, names={"A Friend of the Family"}, text="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker, in the Cathedral (48.5,50.1)", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=48.5, y=50.1},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={98219}, names={"The Shamed Lieutenant"}, text="Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker (new in Forever). A letter job for Southshore: keep it until segment 11", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=48.5, y=50.1},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={387}, names={"Quell The Uprising"}, text="Warden Thelwater, at the Stockade door. Kill 10 Defias Prisoners, 8 Convicts and 8 Insurgents.", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=41.1, y=58.1, dg=3},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1274}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Thomas, the altar boy in the Cathedral", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=49.6, y=44.5},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1274}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Bishop DeLavey, back in Stormwind Keep (80.2,44.1)", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=80.2, y=44.1},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1241}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Bishop DeLavey", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=80.2, y=44.1},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={388}, names={"The Color of Blood"}, text="Nikova Raskol. 10 Red Wool Bandanas from the Defias inside.", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=73.4, y=50.7, dg=3},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1241}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Jorgen, near the main gate at the Valley of Heroes (76.3,85.1)", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=76.3, y=85.1},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1242}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Jorgen", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=76.3, y=85.1},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={1242}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Elling Trias, in the cheese shop in the Trade District (66.0,74.1)", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=66.0, y=74.1},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={1243}, names={"The Missing Diplomat"}, text="Elling Trias. The note goes to Watcher Backus in Darkshire", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=66.0, y=74.1},
  {t="FLY", seg=10, arg="Sentinel Hill", text="Dungar Longdrink, Trade District", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=71.0, y=72.5},
  {t="N", seg=10, arg="Optional dungeon: The Stockade, levels 24-32", text="The Stockade is in Stormwind; Warden Thelwater stands at its door. He also gives The Stockade Riots (Bazil Thredd's head), but only at the end of the long Defias chain that starts with The Unsent Letter from the Deadmines. Quests you picked up for it: What Comes Around..., Crime and Punishment, The Color of Blood, Quell The Uprising. Needs an earlier quest chain this route does not do: The Fury Runs Deep.", zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=41.1, y=58.1, dg=3, run=true},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={387}, names={"Quell The Uprising"}, zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=41.1, y=58.1, dg=3},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={388}, names={"The Color of Blood"}, zone="Stormwind City", map=1453, x=73.4, y=50.7, dg=3},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={67}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="Ride south-west to Moonbrook. The Old Footlocker is inside the schoolhouse (41.5,66.7). Defias (level 15-20) are no danger now", zone="Westfall", map=1436, x=41.5, y=66.7},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={68}, names={"The Legend of Stalvan"}, text="The same footlocker", zone="Westfall", map=1436, x=41.5, y=66.7},
  {t="C", seg=10, q={94502}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Stendel's Pond is just north-east of Moonbrook. Stand by the Forgotten Shrine on the shore (45.5,59.7), eat and drink to full, then drink the Water Sapta: the Corrupt Manifestation of Water becomes visible. Its level is not in the data: open with Stoneclaw Totem and Searing Totem, Earth Shock its casts, Healing Wave early. Loot the Corrupt Manifestation's Bracers", zone="Westfall", map=1436, x=45.5, y=59.7},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={94502}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Click the Forgotten Shrine: it takes the bracers and the Remaining Drops of Purest Water", zone="Westfall", map=1436, x=45.5, y=59.7},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={94503}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="The Forgotten Shrine", zone="Westfall", map=1436, x=45.5, y=59.7},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={94503}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="The Minor Manifestation of Water appears beside the pond (46.4,59.3)", zone="Westfall", map=1436, x=46.4, y=59.3},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={94505}, names={"Call of Water"}, text="Minor Manifestation of Water. The Shard of Water goes to Norric in Loch Modan at the start of segment 11: that is your Water Totem", zone="Westfall", map=1436, x=46.4, y=59.3},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={240}, names={"Return to Jitters"}, text="Go east over the river into Duskwood; Raven Hill is right behind the bridge. Jitters is in Raven Hill village (18.4,56.4)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=18.4, y=56.4},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={453}, names={"Finding the Shadowy Figure"}, text="Jitters", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=18.4, y=56.4},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={268}, names={"Return to Sven"}, text="Jitters", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=18.4, y=56.4},
  {t="N", seg=10, arg="Watch for two new ghosts all over Duskwood: Ira Valor (in the woods) and Merrick Valor (on the roads)", text="New in Forever. Kill them when you see them: one drops Ira's Dagger, the other Merrick's Bow. Each item starts a quest (right-click it). Their exact spots are not in the data. No ghost found? Then skip the steps for 96137 / 96138 / 98447 in this segment"},
  {t="C", seg=10, q={57}, names={"The Night Watch"}, text="The graveyard just north of Jitters (14-24,40-48): kill 15 Skeletal Fiends and 15 Skeletal Horrors (23-25). They are below your level: pull two at a time with Searing Totem down", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=20.0, y=45.0},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={268}, names={"Return to Sven"}, text="Sven Yorgen, at his camp on the far west side (7.8,34.1)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=7.8, y=34.1},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={323}, names={"Proving Your Worth"}, text="Sven Yorgen", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=7.8, y=34.1},
  {t="C", seg=10, q={323}, names={"Proving Your Worth"}, text="The northern part of the cemetery, around the crypts and the big mausoleum (13-20,27-41): 15 Skeletal Raiders (27-28), 3 Skeletal Healers (26-27), 3 Skeletal Warders (28-29). Earth Shock the Healers' heals and the Warders' bolts. Stay outside the crypts: Morbent Fel's house and the crypt depths are elite territory", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=16.2, y=35.3},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={225}, names={"The Weathered Grave"}, text="A Weathered Grave, at the north edge of the cemetery (17.7,29.1). Needs level 28", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=17.7, y=29.1},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={323}, names={"Proving Your Worth"}, text="Back to Sven Yorgen", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=7.8, y=34.1},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={269}, names={"Seeking Wisdom"}, text="Sven Yorgen. For Stormwind, later in this segment", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=7.8, y=34.1},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={157}, names={"Deliver the Thread"}, text="Abercrombie, the hermit in the shack north-east of the cemetery (28.1,31.5). The ghouls around his hill (24-29) attack on sight: go around the east side", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=28.1, y=31.5, path={{7.7,31.6},{13.1,29.8},{16.3,26.8},{24.9,28.9}}},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={158}, names={"Zombie Juice"}, text="Abercrombie", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=28.1, y=31.5},
  {t="S", seg=10, arg="Darkshire", text="Follow the main road east to Darkshire (Ghost Wolf; ravagers and spiders on the road are grey to green). Bind at the Scarlet Raven Tavern (Innkeeper Trelayne)", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.9, y=44.4, path={{33.4,24.1},{37.2,25.3},{40.8,19.6},{51.4,18.4},{54.6,20.8},{57.0,20.8},{64.6,33.4},{68.0,36.1},{68.0,42.7},{70.0,46.6},{72.4,46.6}}},
  {t="A", seg=10, q={90}, names={"Seasoned Wolf Kabobs"}, text="Chef Grual, in the same tavern: Seasoned Wolf Kabobs. He already has the herbs: he only needs 10 Lean Wolf Flanks", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.8, y=43.5},
  {t="T", seg=10, q={158}, names={"Zombie Juice"}, text="Tavernkeep Smitts, in the tavern", zone="Duskwood", map=1431, x=73.8, y=44.5},
